            <ArticleTitle>Review of studies of healing touch.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>147-54</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To review studies of healing touch and its implications for practice and research.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">A review of the literature from published works, abstracts from conference proceedings, theses, and dissertations was conducted to synthesize information on healing touch. Works available until June 2003 were referenced.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The studies were categorized by target of interventions and outcomes were evaluated.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="FINDINGS AND CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Over 30 studies have been conducted with healing touch as the independent variable. Although no generalizable results were found, a foundation exists for further research to test its benefits.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
